#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""vpn-bot-ufw-apply — the main server's UFW is COMPUTED from the repo and .env.

No hand-typed `ufw allow` (docs/host-state.md#the-firewall-ufw). The rule set is

  modules   one table, MODULE_TABLE below: a module is in the set only while .env
            enables it AND it has no uninstall marker (/etc/vpn-bot/uninstalled/<m>)
              xray          XRAY_PUBLIC_PORT/tcp (XRAY_SERVER_PORT, 443)
              hysteria2     HYSTERIA2_PORT/udp (443)           gate HYSTERIA2_ENABLED
              socks5        SOCKS5_PORT/tcp                    gate SOCKS5_ENABLED
              subscription  SUBSCRIPTION_PUBLIC_PORT/tcp       gate SUBSCRIPTION_ENABLED
              mtproto       MTPROTO_PORT/tcp (8443)            gate MTPROTO_ENABLED
              awg           the AWG ListenPort/udp (awg0.conf, else AWG_ENDPOINT_PORT)
                            + route allow in on <AWG_INTERFACE> out on <WAN> from <AWG_NETWORK>
  ssh       SSH_PORT (scripts/vpn-bot-ssh-port) and, while a migration runs, its other
            port(s): the plan's `listen` set (deploy.sh passes it as --ssh-ports)
  extra     deploy/host/ufw/extra.list  (role|rule|reason, reason >= 20 characters):
            every other rule, and listeners declared closed (`closed <port>/<proto>`)
  policies  deploy/host/ufw/policy (role|incoming|outgoing ...); routed is never touched

Every rule of the set carries the comment 'vpn-bot:<module|ssh|extra>'. `apply`
  adds what is missing (a missing v4 or v6 copy too: one `ufw allow` adds both),
  relabels (adopts) a matching rule without our comment — ufw updates it in place,
  deletes a rule with a vpn-bot: comment that is not in the set, and an UNMARKED
  rule that matches a rule of the table (a module switched off or removed, an old
  ssh port — 22 is the package's) — that is how a protocol's rules leave the host,
  leaves any other unmarked rule alone: a WARN, never deleted.

Access is never at stake:
  * a rule that opens the port sshd REALLY listens on (`sshd -T`, ssh.socket's
    Listen=, `ss` rows of sshd or of PID 1 for a socket port) is never deleted; no
    such port found = nothing is deleted at all, and ufw is not enabled nor the
    incoming policy changed. Before either, every such port is opened as well
    (SSH_PORT alone may not be where ssh is: an inactive ssh.socket, sshd on 22);
  * ufw inactive -> enabled, and a change of the incoming policy, happen under a
    dead-man (as the relay's input filter): DEADMAN_STATE records what was before,
    a transient timer runs `deadman-check` every minute, and the change stays only
    with a proof that the ssh port still answers from outside — a NEW connection
    from a non-local address on it in the sshd log (`vpn-bot-ssh-port proof-journal`,
    the proof of the SSH port migration), or «Подтвердить» in the bot (`confirm`).
    Without one, DEADMAN_SECONDS after the change, the previous incoming policy (and
    an inactive ufw) is restored — verified; a revert that failed stays pending and
    is retried at the next check. vpn-bot-ufw-deadman.service (pulled in by the host
    check: 5 min after boot, daily) does the same after a reboot. An ordinary deploy
    changes no policy and needs no dead-man.

Listeners (`listeners`, also in `plan`): every TCP LISTEN on a public or wildcard
address must be allowed by the set or declared closed in extra.list. UDP is checked
only on the UDP ports of the module table; every other UDP socket — the listen-port
of an awg/wg interface (`awg show all listen-port`: kernel-owned, random), outgoing
sockets on a private address — is an INFO line, never an error.

Usage (root; `plan`, `listeners` and `status` only read):
  vpn-bot-ufw-apply plan [--ssh-ports P[,P]]        key=value lines: the decision
  vpn-bot-ufw-apply apply [--ssh-ports P[,P]]       converge the host on the set
  vpn-bot-ufw-apply listeners [--ssh-ports P[,P]]   the listener check alone
  vpn-bot-ufw-apply status                          one line (DEPLOY OK, the bot)
  vpn-bot-ufw-apply save --dir DIR                  snapshot for a rollback (deploy.sh)
  vpn-bot-ufw-apply restore --dir DIR               put that snapshot back
  vpn-bot-ufw-apply deadman-check                   the timer / the boot run
  vpn-bot-ufw-apply confirm --since EPOCH --admin ID     the bot's «Подтвердить»
Common options: --env FILE (/opt/vpn-service/.env), --repo DIR (/opt/vpn-service:
deploy/host/ufw/*), --root DIR (tests: host files under DIR), --ssh-port-helper PATH
(/usr/local/sbin/vpn-bot-ssh-port).

Exit codes: 0 ok; 2 usage; 3 refused (extra.list/policy/.env invalid, not main);
4 apply did not converge, or a listener check failed; 5 cannot run (ufw missing, a
tool or a file); 9 the dead-man could not be armed (the policy is left as it was).

Never evaluates command output; every command is an argv list. Stdlib only. Run
as root from another mount namespace (the non-root bot's ProtectSystem=strict, which
sudo keeps) a writing command re-executes itself in PID 1's first (nsenter): /etc/ufw
must be writable. TEST SEAM: VPN_BOT_UFW_SELFTEST=1 needs --root and makes every
command resolve inside VPN_BOT_UFW_SELFTEST_BIN — a missing stub never reaches a
real ufw (deploy.sh runs the test suite as root on the production host).
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import contextlib
import fcntl
import ipaddress
import json
import os
import re
import shlex
import shutil
import subprocess  # noqa: S404 — fixed argv lists of system tools, never a shell
import sys
import tempfile
import time
from collections.abc import Iterator, Sequence
from dataclasses import dataclass, field, replace
from pathlib import Path
from typing import Any

APP_DIR = "/opt/vpn-service"
INSTALLED_PATH = "/usr/local/sbin/vpn-bot-ufw-apply"
SSH_PORT_HELPER = "/usr/local/sbin/vpn-bot-ssh-port"
EXTRA_LIST = "deploy/host/ufw/extra.list"
POLICY_FILE = "deploy/host/ufw/policy"
MARKER_DIR = "/etc/vpn-bot/uninstalled"
UFW_DEFAULTS = "/etc/default/ufw"
UFW_CONF = "/etc/ufw/ufw.conf"
USER_RULES = "/etc/ufw/user.rules"
USER6_RULES = "/etc/ufw/user6.rules"
SAVED_FILES = (UFW_DEFAULTS, UFW_CONF, USER_RULES, USER6_RULES)
SSHD_CONFIG = "/etc/ssh/sshd_config"
PROC_IPV6 = "/proc/sys/net/ipv6"
SSH_SOCKET = "ssh.socket"
SSH_STATE = "/var/lib/vpn-bot/ssh-migration.json"
DEADMAN_STATE = "/var/lib/vpn-bot/ufw-deadman.json"
DEADMAN_UNIT = "vpn-bot-ufw-deadman-watch"
DEADMAN_SECONDS = 600
DEADMAN_INTERVAL = 60
LOCK_FILE = "/run/vpn-bot-ufw-apply.lock"
COMMENT_PREFIX = "vpn-bot:"
# A rule for this port without our comment is ssh's: the port the package listens on.
SSH_PACKAGE_PORT = 22
SSH_DEFAULT = 54321                 # SSH_PORT absent (scripts/vpn-bot-ssh-port)
AWG_CONFIG_DEFAULT = "/etc/amnezia/amneziawg/awg0.conf"
REASON_MIN = 20
COMMAND_TIMEOUT = 60
EXIT_REFUSED = 3
EXIT_NOT_CONVERGED = 4
EXIT_CANNOT = 5
EXIT_DEADMAN = 9

SELFTEST = os.environ.get("VPN_BOT_UFW_SELFTEST") == "1"

POLICY_OF_IPT = {"DROP": "deny", "ACCEPT": "allow", "REJECT": "reject"}
POLICIES = frozenset({"allow", "deny", "reject"})
DIRECTIONS = ("incoming", "outgoing")
SSH_PROCS = frozenset({"sshd", "sshd-session"})
PORT_RE = re.compile(r"^[1-9][0-9]{0,4}$")
LISTEN_RE = re.compile(r"^Listen=(.*):(\d+) \(Stream\)$")
USERS_RE = re.compile(r'\("([^"]+)",pid=(\d+)')
ACTIONS = frozenset({"allow", "deny", "reject", "limit"})
PROTOS = frozenset({"tcp", "udp", "ah", "esp", "gre", "ipv6", "igmp"})
KEYWORDS = frozenset({"in", "out", "on", "from", "to", "port", "proto", "app", "log", "log-all"})


class Refused(Exception):
    """The set cannot be computed: the reason is for the operator."""


class Cannot(Exception):
    """A tool or a file the helper needs failed."""


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Context
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
@dataclass
class Ctx:
    env_file: Path
    repo: Path
    root: str
    ssh_helper: str
    env_text: str = ""

    def host(self, path: str) -> Path:
        return Path(f"{self.root}{path}")

    def env(self, key: str) -> str:
        return env_sed_val(self.env_text, key)


def env_sed_val(text: str, key: str) -> str:
    """scripts/deploy.sh's env_sed_val: optional `export`, spaces around `=`, an inline
    `# comment`, double then single quotes, the last assignment wins."""
    rx = re.compile(r"^\s*(?:export\s+)?" + re.escape(key) + r"\s*=\s*(.*)$")
    val: str | None = None
    for line in text.split("\n"):
        m = rx.match(line)
        if m:
            val = m.group(1)
    if val is None:
        return ""
    val = re.sub(r"\s*#.*$", "", val)
    for q in ('"', "'"):
        if len(val) >= 2 and val.startswith(q) and val.endswith(q):
            val = val[1:-1]
    return val.rstrip()


def is_true(value: str) -> bool:
    """config/settings.py's _bool: what the application itself treats as switched on."""
    return value.strip().lower() in ("1", "true", "yes", "y", "on")


def tool_allowed(name: str) -> str | None:
    """Under the test seam, the stub's path; None = refused. Outside it, the name."""
    if not SELFTEST:
        return name
    stub_dir = os.environ.get("VPN_BOT_UFW_SELFTEST_BIN", "")
    found = shutil.which(name)
    if not stub_dir or not found:
        return None
    if os.path.realpath(found) != os.path.realpath(os.path.join(stub_dir, name)):
        return None
    return found


def run(argv: Sequence[str], *, timeout: int = COMMAND_TIMEOUT) -> tuple[int, str]:
    """(exit code, stdout+stderr); 127 = not found (or refused by the test seam)."""
    args = list(argv)
    if args[0] != sys.executable:
        exe = tool_allowed(args[0])
        if exe is None:
            return 127, f"{args[0]}: refused (VPN_BOT_UFW_SELFTEST: not a stub in VPN_BOT_UFW_SELFTEST_BIN)"
        args[0] = exe
    try:
        proc = subprocess.run(args, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout, check=False)  # noqa: S603
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return 127, f"{argv[0]}: not found"
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        return 124, f"{argv[0]}: timed out after {timeout}s"
    return proc.returncode, proc.stdout + proc.stderr


def out_of(argv: Sequence[str], *, timeout: int = COMMAND_TIMEOUT) -> str | None:
    """stdout+stderr of a command that must succeed, or None."""
    rc, text = run(argv, timeout=timeout)
    return text if rc == 0 else None


def csv(ports: Sequence[int]) -> str:
    return ",".join(str(p) for p in ports)


def parse_ports(text: str) -> list[int]:
    out: set[int] = set()
    for part in re.split(r"[,\s]+", text.strip()):
        if PORT_RE.match(part) and int(part) <= 65535:
            out.add(int(part))
    return sorted(out)


def port_of(raw: str) -> int | None:
    return int(raw) if PORT_RE.match(raw) and int(raw) <= 65535 else None


def iso(ts: float) -> str:
    return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(ts))


def one(text: str) -> str:
    return text.replace("\n", " ").replace("\r", " ").replace("|", "/")


def fence(ctx: Ctx, path: Path) -> None:
    """Under VPN_BOT_UFW_SELFTEST=1 nothing outside --root is ever written."""
    if SELFTEST and (not ctx.root or not str(path).startswith(ctx.root.rstrip("/") + "/")):
        raise Cannot(f"selftest: refusing to write {path} outside --root {ctx.root!r}")


def read_text(path: Path) -> str | None:
    """A regular file's text; None when absent. A symlink is never followed."""
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return None
    except OSError as exc:
        raise Cannot(f"cannot read {path}: {exc}") from exc
    with os.fdopen(fd, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace", newline="") as fh:
        return fh.read()


def write_atomic(ctx: Ctx, path: Path, data: str, mode: int = 0o644) -> None:
    """A temporary file in the same directory (never follows a planted link), then rename."""
    fence(ctx, path)
    path.parent.mkdir(mode=0o755, parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=str(path.parent), prefix=f".{path.name}.")
    try:
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            fh.write(data)
            fh.flush()
            os.fsync(fh.fileno())
        os.chmod(tmp, mode)
        if os.geteuid() == 0 and not SELFTEST:
            os.chown(tmp, 0, 0)
        os.replace(tmp, path)
    except BaseException:
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            os.unlink(tmp)
        raise


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# A UFW rule as a key: what `ufw show added` prints and what /etc/ufw/user*.rules
# record (### tuple ###) map to the same Key, so v4 and v6 copies can be counted.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
@dataclass(frozen=True)
class Key:
    route: bool = False
    action: str = "allow"      # allow | deny | reject | limit
    log: str = ""              # "" | log | log-all
    direction: str = "in"      # in | out
    iface_in: str = ""
    iface_out: str = ""
    src: str = "any"
    sport: str = "any"
    dst: str = "any"
    dport: str = "any"
    proto: str = "any"
    sapp: str = ""
    dapp: str = ""


def norm_addr(addr: str) -> str:
    if addr in ("any", "0.0.0.0/0", "::/0"):
        return "any"
    try:
        net = ipaddress.ip_network(addr, strict=False)
    except ValueError:
        return addr
    if net.prefixlen == net.max_prefixlen:
        return str(net.network_address)
    return str(net)


def addr_family(addr: str) -> str:
    """v4 | v6 | "" (any, or not an address)."""
    if addr == "any":
        return ""
    try:
        return "v6" if ipaddress.ip_network(addr, strict=False).version == 6 else "v4"
    except ValueError:
        return ""


def families_of(key: Key, ipv6: bool) -> frozenset[str]:
    """The copies ufw keeps of this rule: one per address family it can apply to."""
    fams = {addr_family(key.src), addr_family(key.dst)} - {""}
    if fams:
        return frozenset(fams)
    return frozenset({"v4", "v6"} if ipv6 else {"v4"})


def rule_text(key: Key) -> str:
    """ufw's own UFWCommandRule.get_command (ufw 0.36), without the comment: the text
    `ufw show added` prints, and the argv `ufw` takes."""
    res = key.action
    if key.src == "any" and key.dst == "any" and key.sport == "any" and not key.sapp \
            and not key.iface_in and not key.iface_out and key.dport != "any":
        if key.direction == "out":
            res += " out"
        if key.log:
            res += f" {key.log}"
        if key.dapp:
            res += f" '{key.dapp}'" if " " in key.dapp else f" {key.dapp}"
        else:
            res += f" {key.dport}"
            if key.proto != "any":
                res += f"/{key.proto}"
    else:
        if key.iface_in:
            res += f" in on {key.iface_in}"
        if key.iface_out:
            res += f" out on {key.iface_out}"
        elif key.direction == "out":
            res += " out"
        if key.log:
            res += f" {key.log}"
        for word, loc, port, app in (("from", key.src, key.sport, key.sapp), ("to", key.dst, key.dport, key.dapp)):
            if loc != "any" or port != "any" or app:
                res += f" {word} {loc}"
                if app:
                    res += f" app '{app}'" if " " in app else f" app {app}"
                elif port != "any":
                    res += f" port {port}"
        if " to " not in res and " from " not in res and not key.iface_in and not key.iface_out:
            res += " to any"
        if key.proto != "any" and not key.dapp and not key.sapp:
            res += f" proto {key.proto}"
    return ("route " + res) if key.route else res


def parse_rule(text: str) -> Key | None:
    """The Key of a rule as `ufw show added` prints it (without "ufw " and the comment);
    None when it is not one of the shapes ufw prints."""
    try:
        toks = shlex.split(text)
    except ValueError:
        return None
    if toks and toks[0] == "ufw":
        toks = toks[1:]
    route = bool(toks) and toks[0] == "route"
    if route:
        toks = toks[1:]
    if not toks or toks[0] not in ACTIONS:
        return None
    k: dict[str, Any] = {"route": route, "action": toks[0]}
    rest = toks[1:]
    # Short syntax: [out] [log|log-all] PORT[/PROTO] | APP
    j = 0
    short: dict[str, Any] = {}
    if j < len(rest) and rest[j] in ("in", "out") and (j + 1 >= len(rest) or rest[j + 1] != "on"):
        short["direction"] = rest[j]
        j += 1
    if j < len(rest) and rest[j] in ("log", "log-all"):
        short["log"] = rest[j]
        j += 1
    if len(rest) - j == 1 and rest[j] not in KEYWORDS:
        m = re.fullmatch(r"([0-9][0-9,:]*)(?:/([a-z0-9]+))?", rest[j])
        if m:
            if m.group(2) and m.group(2) not in PROTOS:
                return None
            short.update(dport=m.group(1), proto=m.group(2) or "any")
        else:
            short["dapp"] = rest[j]
        return Key(**k, **short)
    # Full syntax
    saw_in = saw_out = False
    i = 0
    while i < len(rest):
        t = rest[i]
        if t in ("in", "out"):
            if i + 1 < len(rest) and rest[i + 1] == "on":
                if i + 2 >= len(rest):
                    return None
                k["iface_in" if t == "in" else "iface_out"] = rest[i + 2]
                i += 3
            else:
                i += 1
            if t == "in":
                saw_in = True
            else:
                saw_out = True
        elif t in ("log", "log-all"):
            k["log"] = t
            i += 1
        elif t in ("from", "to"):
            if i + 1 >= len(rest):
                return None
            side = "s" if t == "from" else "d"
            k["src" if side == "s" else "dst"] = norm_addr(rest[i + 1])
            i += 2
            if i + 1 < len(rest) and rest[i] == "port":
                k[f"{side}port"] = rest[i + 1]
                i += 2
            elif i + 1 < len(rest) and rest[i] == "app":
                k[f"{side}app"] = rest[i + 1]
                i += 2
        elif t == "proto":
            if i + 1 >= len(rest) or rest[i + 1] not in PROTOS:
                return None
            k["proto"] = rest[i + 1]
            i += 2
        else:
            return None
    k["direction"] = "out" if saw_out and not saw_in else "in"
    return Key(**k)


def hex_decode(text: str) -> str:
    try:
        return bytes.fromhex(text).decode("utf-8", errors="replace")
    except ValueError:
        return ""


def parse_tuple(line: str) -> tuple[Key, str] | None:
    """(key, comment) of a `### tuple ###` line of /etc/ufw/user*.rules."""
    line = line.rstrip("\n")
    comment = ""
    if " comment=" in line:
        line, hexed = line.split(" comment=", 1)
        comment = hex_decode(hexed.strip())
    m = re.match(r"^### tuple ###\s*(.*)$", line)
    if not m:
        return None
    tmp = m.group(1).split()
    if len(tmp) not in (7, 9):
        return None
    action, route = tmp[0], False
    if ":" in action:
        route, action = True, action.split(":", 1)[1]
    log = ""
    if "_" in action:
        action, log = action.split("_", 1)
    if action not in ACTIONS:
        return None
    dapp = sapp = ""
    if len(tmp) == 9:
        dapp = "" if tmp[6] == "-" else tmp[6].replace("%20", " ")
        sapp = "" if tmp[7] == "-" else tmp[7].replace("%20", " ")
    ifaces = tmp[-1]
    direction = ifaces.split("_", 1)[0].split("!", 1)[0]
    iface_in = iface_out = ""
    if "!" in ifaces:
        a, b = ifaces.split("!", 1)
        iface_in, iface_out = a.partition("_")[2], b.partition("_")[2]
    elif "_" in ifaces:
        d, _, ifc = ifaces.partition("_")
        if d == "in":
            iface_in = ifc
        else:
            iface_out = ifc
    if direction not in ("in", "out"):
        return None
    key = Key(route=route, action=action, log=log, direction=direction, iface_in=iface_in, iface_out=iface_out,
              src=norm_addr(tmp[5]), sport=tmp[4], dst=norm_addr(tmp[3]), dport=tmp[2], proto=tmp[1],
              sapp=sapp, dapp=dapp)
    return key, comment


def port_covered(spec: str, port: int) -> bool:
    """Does a ufw port spec ("443", "80,443", "6000:6007") contain <port>?"""
    if spec == "any":
        return True
    for part in spec.split(","):
        lo, _, hi = part.partition(":")
        if not lo.isdigit() or (hi and not hi.isdigit()):
            continue
        if int(lo) <= port <= int(hi or lo):
            return True
    return False


def opens(key: Key, port: int, proto: str) -> bool:
    """Does this rule let <port>/<proto> in from anywhere or from somewhere?"""
    return (not key.route and key.direction == "in" and key.action in ("allow", "limit")
            and not key.dapp and key.proto in ("any", proto) and port_covered(key.dport, port))


def simple(port: int, proto: str) -> Key:
    return Key(dport=str(port), proto=proto)


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The module table — the ONE place a module's rules are written down. The set uses
# it for the modules that are on; recognition of unmarked rules uses it for all of
# them (a module switched off or removed included); the listener check takes its
# UDP ports from it. deploy/helpers/vpn-bot-protocol-uninstall knows no port: the
# marker it writes takes the module out of the set, the bot runs `apply`.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
@dataclass(frozen=True)
class Module:
    name: str
    gate: str            # the .env flag ("" = none: on unless removed)
    marker: str          # its uninstall marker ("" = it cannot be removed)
    proto: str           # of its port rule
    port_keys: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    port_default: str = ""
    route: bool = False  # AWG: the route rule of its clients to the internet


MODULE_TABLE: tuple[Module, ...] = (
    Module("xray", "", "xray", "tcp", ("XRAY_PUBLIC_PORT", "XRAY_SERVER_PORT"), "443"),
    Module("hysteria2", "HYSTERIA2_ENABLED", "hysteria2", "udp", ("HYSTERIA2_PORT",), "443"),
    Module("socks5", "SOCKS5_ENABLED", "socks5", "tcp", ("SOCKS5_PORT",), ""),
    Module("subscription", "SUBSCRIPTION_ENABLED", "", "tcp", ("SUBSCRIPTION_PUBLIC_PORT",), "0"),
    Module("mtproto", "MTPROTO_ENABLED", "mtproto", "tcp", ("MTPROTO_PORT",), "8443"),
    Module("awg", "", "awg", "udp", (), "", route=True),
)


@dataclass
class ModuleState:
    module: Module
    on: bool
    why: str                          # "on" | ".env: X=false" | "removed (marker)"
    port: int | None = None
    port_why: str = ""
    route_in: str = ""                # AWG: interface and client network
    route_src: str = ""
    route_out: str = ""               # the WAN interface ("" = unknown)
    notes: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)
    # On, but a rule of it cannot be written down here (a port or the WAN unknown): what
    # is recognisably its own stays. Not set for a port that is off by design (0).
    incomplete: bool = False

    def keys(self) -> list[tuple[Key, str]]:
        """The rules of this module that can be written down here, with why."""
        out: list[tuple[Key, str]] = []
        if self.port is not None:
            out.append((simple(self.port, self.module.proto), self.port_why))
        if self.module.route and self.route_in and self.route_src and self.route_out:
            out.append((Key(route=True, iface_in=self.route_in, iface_out=self.route_out, src=self.route_src),
                        f"AWG clients ({self.route_src} on {self.route_in}) to the internet via {self.route_out}"))
        return out

    def matches(self, key: Key) -> bool:
        """Is <key> a rule of this module (an unmarked rule recognised as ours)?"""
        if self.port is not None and key == simple(self.port, self.module.proto):
            return True
        if self.module.route and self.route_in and self.route_src:
            return (key.route and key.action == "allow" and key.iface_in == self.route_in
                    and key.src == self.route_src and key.dst == "any" and key.sport == "any"
                    and key.dport == "any" and key.proto == "any" and not key.sapp and not key.dapp)
        return False


def awg_listen_port(ctx: Ctx) -> int | None:
    path = ctx.env("AWG_CONFIG_PATH") or AWG_CONFIG_DEFAULT
    try:
        text = read_text(ctx.host(path)) or ""
    except Cannot:
        return None
    section = ""
    for line in text.splitlines():
        s = line.strip()
        if s.startswith("["):
            section = s.lower()
            continue
        m = re.match(r"^ListenPort\s*=\s*(\S+)", s)
        if m and section == "[interface]":
            return port_of(m.group(1))
    return None


def wan_interface() -> str:
    out = out_of(["ip", "-4", "route", "show", "default"]) or ""
    m = re.search(r"\bdev (\S+)", out)
    return m.group(1) if m else ""


def module_states(ctx: Ctx) -> list[ModuleState]:
    wan: str | None = None
    states: list[ModuleState] = []
    for mod in MODULE_TABLE:
        on, why = True, "on"
        if mod.gate and not is_true(ctx.env(mod.gate)):
            on, why = False, f".env: {mod.gate}={ctx.env(mod.gate) or '<unset>'}"
        if mod.marker and ctx.host(f"{MARKER_DIR}/{mod.marker}").is_file():
            on, why = False, f"removed from this host (marker {MARKER_DIR}/{mod.marker})"
        st = ModuleState(mod, on, why)
        if mod.name == "awg":
            port = awg_listen_port(ctx)
            if port is not None:
                st.port, st.port_why = port, "ListenPort of the AWG config"
            else:
                raw = ctx.env("AWG_ENDPOINT_PORT")
                p = port_of(raw)
                if p is not None:
                    st.port, st.port_why = p, f"AWG_ENDPOINT_PORT={p}"
                elif on:
                    st.incomplete = True
                    st.notes.append("the AWG listen port is unknown (no ListenPort in the AWG config, no "
                                    "AWG_ENDPOINT_PORT) — its udp rule is not managed")
            st.route_in = ctx.env("AWG_INTERFACE") or "awg0"
            st.route_src = norm_addr(ctx.env("AWG_NETWORK") or "10.0.0.0/24")
            if on:
                wan = wan_interface() if wan is None else wan
                st.route_out = wan
                if not wan:
                    st.incomplete = True
                    st.notes.append("no IPv4 default route (`ip -4 route show default`) — the AWG route rule "
                                    "cannot be written down: not managed")
        else:
            raw, key_used = "", ""
            for k in mod.port_keys:
                raw = ctx.env(k)
                if raw:
                    key_used = k
                    break
            if not raw:
                raw, key_used = mod.port_default, f"{mod.port_keys[0]} (default)"
            if raw in ("", "0"):
                if on:
                    st.notes.append(f"{mod.port_keys[0]} is not set — {mod.name} has no public port to open")
                    # "0" is off by design (SUBSCRIPTION_PUBLIC_PORT); an empty port of a module
                    # that needs one (SOCKS5_PORT) is a port nobody can tell.
                    st.incomplete = raw == "" and mod.port_default != "0"
            else:
                p = port_of(raw)
                if p is None:
                    if on:
                        raise Refused(f"{key_used}={raw!r} in {ctx.env_file} is not a port ({mod.name} is on)")
                else:
                    st.port, st.port_why = p, f"{key_used.split(' ')[0]}={p}"
        states.append(st)
    return states


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# deploy/host/ufw/extra.list and deploy/host/ufw/policy
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
@dataclass(frozen=True)
class Extra:
    key: Key | None          # an extra rule ...
    closed: tuple[int, str] | None   # ... or a listener declared closed: (port, proto)
    reason: str
    line: int


def read_extra(ctx: Ctx) -> list[Extra]:
    path = ctx.repo / EXTRA_LIST
    text = read_text(path)
    if text is None:
        raise Refused(f"{path} is missing — the rules of no module go there; an empty list is a file with comments")
    out: list[Extra] = []
    seen: set[str] = set()
    for n, raw in enumerate(text.splitlines(), 1):
        line = raw.strip()
        if not line or line.startswith("#"):
            continue
        parts = line.split("|", 2)
        if len(parts) != 3:
            raise Refused(f"{EXTRA_LIST}:{n}: not 'role|rule|reason': {line!r}")
        role, rule, reason = (p.strip() for p in parts)
        if role not in ("main", "relay"):
            raise Refused(f"{EXTRA_LIST}:{n}: role {role!r} is not main or relay")
        if len(reason) < REASON_MIN:
            raise Refused(f"{EXTRA_LIST}:{n}: the reason must say why in at least {REASON_MIN} characters: {reason!r}")
        if rule in seen:
            raise Refused(f"{EXTRA_LIST}:{n}: {rule!r} is listed twice")
        seen.add(rule)
        if role != "main":
            continue
        m = re.fullmatch(r"closed\s+([0-9]+)/(tcp|udp)", rule)
        if m:
            port = port_of(m.group(1))
            if port is None:
                raise Refused(f"{EXTRA_LIST}:{n}: {m.group(1)!r} is not a port")
            out.append(Extra(None, (port, m.group(2)), reason, n))
            continue
        if " comment " in f" {rule} ":
            raise Refused(f"{EXTRA_LIST}:{n}: no comment in the rule — the helper writes 'vpn-bot:extra'")
        key = parse_rule(rule)
        if key is None or key.dapp or key.sapp:
            raise Refused(f"{EXTRA_LIST}:{n}: {rule!r} is not a ufw rule as `ufw show added` prints it "
                          "(no application profiles), nor 'closed <port>/<tcp|udp>'")
        out.append(Extra(key, None, reason, n))
    return out


def read_policy(ctx: Ctx) -> dict[str, str]:
    path = ctx.repo / POLICY_FILE
    text = read_text(path)
    if text is None:
        raise Refused(f"{path} is missing — the default policies are written down there")
    out: dict[str, str] = {}
    for n, raw in enumerate(text.splitlines(), 1):
        line = raw.strip()
        if not line or line.startswith("#"):
            continue
        parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split("|")]
        if len(parts) != 3:
            raise Refused(f"{POLICY_FILE}:{n}: not 'role|direction|policy': {line!r}")
        role, direction, policy = parts
        if role not in ("main", "relay"):
            raise Refused(f"{POLICY_FILE}:{n}: role {role!r} is not main or relay")
        if direction == "routed":
            raise Refused(f"{POLICY_FILE}:{n}: the routed policy is never managed (AWG and WARP forwarding live "
                          "on route rules) — drop the line")
        if direction not in DIRECTIONS:
            raise Refused(f"{POLICY_FILE}:{n}: direction {direction!r} is not incoming or outgoing")
        if policy not in POLICIES:
            raise Refused(f"{POLICY_FILE}:{n}: policy {policy!r} is not allow, deny or reject")
        if role == "main":
            if direction in out:
                raise Refused(f"{POLICY_FILE}:{n}: {direction} is set twice")
            out[direction] = policy
    return out


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The host: ufw, its files, ssh, listeners
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
@dataclass
class Rule:
    text: str
    comment: str
    key: Key | None
    families: frozenset[str] = frozenset()


@dataclass
class UfwState:
    present: bool = False
    active: bool | None = None
    ipv6: bool = True
    policies: dict[str, str] = field(default_factory=dict)   # incoming/outgoing/routed -> allow|deny|reject
    rules: list[Rule] = field(default_factory=list)
    families_known: bool = False
    error: str = ""


SHOW_RE = re.compile(r"^ufw (?P<rule>.*?)(?: comment '(?P<comment>.*)')?$")


def read_defaults(ctx: Ctx) -> dict[str, str]:
    text = read_text(ctx.host(UFW_DEFAULTS)) or ""
    out: dict[str, str] = {}
    for line in text.splitlines():
        m = re.match(r'^\s*([A-Z0-9_]+)\s*=\s*"?([^"#]*?)"?\s*(?:#.*)?$', line)
        if m:
            out[m.group(1)] = m.group(2)
    return out


def read_tuples(ctx: Ctx) -> dict[Key, set[str]] | None:
    """Key -> the families it has a copy in; None when the files cannot be read."""
    fams: dict[Key, set[str]] = {}
    for path, fam in ((USER_RULES, "v4"), (USER6_RULES, "v6")):
        try:
            text = read_text(ctx.host(path))
        except Cannot:
            return None
        if text is None:
            if fam == "v4":
                return None
            continue
        for line in text.splitlines():
            parsed = parse_tuple(line)
            if parsed is not None:
                fams.setdefault(parsed[0], set()).add(fam)
    return fams


def read_ufw(ctx: Ctx) -> UfwState:
    st = UfwState()
    rc, text = run(["ufw", "status"])
    if rc == 127:
        st.error = "ufw is not installed"
        return st
    st.present = True
    if rc != 0:
        st.error = f"`ufw status` failed (rc {rc}): {one(text.strip())}"
        return st
    m = re.search(r"^Status: (active|inactive)", text, re.M)
    st.active = None if m is None else m.group(1) == "active"
    d = read_defaults(ctx)
    # ufw's own use_ipv6(): IPV6=yes AND a kernel with IPv6 — else it keeps no v6 copies.
    st.ipv6 = d.get("IPV6", "yes").lower() == "yes" and ctx.host(PROC_IPV6).exists()
    for name, var in (("incoming", "DEFAULT_INPUT_POLICY"), ("outgoing", "DEFAULT_OUTPUT_POLICY"),
                      ("routed", "DEFAULT_FORWARD_POLICY")):
        st.policies[name] = POLICY_OF_IPT.get(d.get(var, "").upper(), d.get(var, "") or "?")
    rc, text = run(["ufw", "show", "added"])
    if rc != 0:
        st.error = f"`ufw show added` failed (rc {rc}): {one(text.strip())}"
        return st
    tuples = read_tuples(ctx)
    st.families_known = tuples is not None
    for line in text.splitlines():
        m2 = SHOW_RE.match(line.strip())
        if not m2:
            continue
        rtext = m2.group("rule")
        key = parse_rule(rtext)
        fams: frozenset[str] = frozenset()
        if key is not None and tuples is not None:
            fams = frozenset(tuples.get(key, set()))
        st.rules.append(Rule(rtext, m2.group("comment") or "", key, fams))
    return st


@dataclass
class Listener:
    proto: str
    addr: str
    port: int
    procs: list[tuple[str, int]]


def listeners(proto: str) -> list[Listener] | None:
    out = out_of(["ss", "-Hltnp" if proto == "tcp" else "-Hulnp"])
    if out is None:
        return None
    rows: list[Listener] = []
    for line in out.splitlines():
        toks = line.split()
        if len(toks) < 5:
            continue
        local = toks[3] if toks[0] in ("LISTEN", "UNCONN", "ESTAB") else toks[2]
        addr, _, port = local.rpartition(":")
        if not port.isdigit():
            continue
        rows.append(Listener(proto, addr, int(port), [(m.group(1), int(m.group(2))) for m in USERS_RE.finditer(line)]))
    return rows


def bare_addr(addr: str) -> str:
    a = addr.split("%", 1)[0].strip("[]")
    try:
        ip = ipaddress.ip_address(a)
    except ValueError:
        return a
    if isinstance(ip, ipaddress.IPv6Address) and ip.ipv4_mapped is not None:
        return str(ip.ipv4_mapped)
    return str(ip)


def is_public(addr: str) -> bool:
    a = bare_addr(addr)
    if a in ("*", "0.0.0.0", "::", ""):  # noqa: S104 — classifying an address, not binding
        return True
    try:
        return ipaddress.ip_address(a).is_global
    except ValueError:
        return False


def is_loopback(addr: str) -> bool:
    try:
        return ipaddress.ip_address(bare_addr(addr)).is_loopback
    except ValueError:
        return False


def socket_ports() -> list[int]:
    out = out_of(["systemctl", "show", "-p", "Listen", SSH_SOCKET]) or ""
    return sorted({int(m.group(2)) for ln in out.splitlines() if (m := LISTEN_RE.match(ln.strip()))})


def sshd_ports(ctx: Ctx) -> list[int]:
    out = out_of(["sshd", "-T", "-f", str(ctx.host(SSHD_CONFIG))]) or ""
    return sorted({int(ln.split()[1]) for ln in out.splitlines() if re.match(r"^port \d+$", ln.strip())})


def live_ssh_ports(ctx: Ctx, tcp: list[Listener] | None) -> tuple[list[int], str]:
    """The ports sshd really listens on, and where that came from. A union of every
    source: the safe direction is a port too many, never one too few."""
    sock = socket_ports()
    sshd = sshd_ports(ctx)
    held = sorted({r.port for r in tcp or [] for name, pid in r.procs
                   if name in SSH_PROCS or (name == "systemd" and pid == 1 and r.port in sock)})
    ports = sorted({*sock, *sshd, *held})
    why = f"ssh.socket {csv(sock) or '-'}, sshd -T {csv(sshd) or '-'}, ss {csv(held) or '-'}"
    return ports, why


def kernel_udp_ports() -> dict[int, str]:
    """port -> interface: the listen-port of every awg/wg interface (no process owns it)."""
    ports: dict[int, str] = {}
    for tool in ("awg", "wg"):
        out = out_of([tool, "show", "all", "listen-port"]) or ""
        for line in out.splitlines():
            parts = line.split()
            if len(parts) == 2 and parts[1].isdigit() and int(parts[1]) > 0:
                ports.setdefault(int(parts[1]), f"{parts[0]} ({tool})")
    return ports


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# SSH ports for the set
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def ssh_plan(ctx: Ctx) -> dict[str, str]:
    helper = ctx.ssh_helper
    if not helper or not os.path.isfile(helper):
        return {}
    argv = [sys.executable, "-I", helper, "--env", str(ctx.env_file), "--repo", str(ctx.repo), "--role", "main"]
    if ctx.root:
        argv += ["--root", ctx.root]
    rc, text = run([*argv, "plan"], timeout=180)
    plan = {ln.split("=", 1)[0]: ln.split("=", 1)[1] for ln in text.splitlines() if "=" in ln}
    return plan if rc in (0, 3) else {}


def ssh_desired(ctx: Ctx, given: str | None) -> tuple[list[int], str, list[int]]:
    """(the ssh ports of the set, where they came from, other ssh ports this host had)."""
    known: set[int] = {SSH_PACKAGE_PORT}
    with contextlib.suppress(Cannot, ValueError, TypeError, KeyError):
        data = json.loads(read_text(ctx.host(SSH_STATE)) or "{}")
        known.update(int(p) for p in data.get("from", []))
        if data.get("to"):
            known.add(int(data["to"]))
    if given:
        ports = parse_ports(given)
        if ports:
            return ports, "the deploy's SSH port plan", sorted(known)
    plan = ssh_plan(ctx)
    if plan.get("action") not in (None, "", "refused") and parse_ports(plan.get("listen", "")):
        known.update(parse_ports(plan.get("from", "")))
        return parse_ports(plan["listen"]), f"vpn-bot-ssh-port plan ({plan['action']})", sorted(known)
    raw = ctx.env("SSH_PORT")
    port = port_of(raw) if raw else SSH_DEFAULT
    if port is None:
        raise Refused(f"SSH_PORT={raw!r} in {ctx.env_file} is not a port")
    return [port], "SSH_PORT" + (" (default)" if not raw else ""), sorted(known)


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The decision
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
@dataclass
class Want:
    key: Key
    category: str
    why: str

    @property
    def comment(self) -> str:
        return COMMENT_PREFIX + self.category

    @property
    def text(self) -> str:
        return rule_text(self.key)


@dataclass
class Item:
    action: str          # ok | add | adopt | delete | keep | warn
    category: str        # module | ssh | extra | -
    marked: str          # yes | no | - (delete/keep: did it carry a vpn-bot: comment)
    text: str
    detail: str
    want: Want | None = None
    rule: Rule | None = None

    def kv(self) -> str:
        return f"rule={self.action}|{self.category}|{self.marked}|{self.text}|{one(self.detail)}"


@dataclass
class ListenerItem:
    verdict: str         # ok | closed | FAIL | info
    proto: str
    port: int
    addr: str
    detail: str

    def kv(self) -> str:
        return f"listener={self.verdict}|{self.proto}|{self.port}|{self.addr}|{one(self.detail)}"


@dataclass
class Plan:
    ufw: UfwState
    modules: list[ModuleState]
    wants: list[Want]
    items: list[Item]
    policy_want: dict[str, str]
    ssh_ports: list[int]
    ssh_source: str
    live: list[int]
    live_why: str
    closed: list[tuple[int, str]]
    notes: list[str]
    listeners: list[ListenerItem] = field(default_factory=list)
    listeners_known: bool = True

    def count(self, action: str) -> int:
        return sum(1 for i in self.items if i.action == action)

    @property
    def policy_changes(self) -> dict[str, tuple[str, str]]:
        return {d: (self.ufw.policies.get(d, "?"), w) for d, w in self.policy_want.items()
                if self.ufw.policies.get(d) != w}

    @property
    def listener_failures(self) -> list[ListenerItem]:
        return [x for x in self.listeners if x.verdict == "FAIL"]


def protected(key: Key | None, live: list[int]) -> int | None:
    """The live ssh port a rule opens (it is never deleted), or None."""
    if key is None:
        return None
    for p in live:
        if opens(key, p, "tcp"):
            return p
    return None


def compute(ctx: Ctx, ssh_given: str | None, *, with_listeners: bool = True) -> Plan:
    policy_want = read_policy(ctx)
    extras = read_extra(ctx)
    modules = module_states(ctx)
    ssh_ports, ssh_source, ssh_known = ssh_desired(ctx, ssh_given)
    ufw = read_ufw(ctx)
    tcp = listeners("tcp")
    live, live_why = live_ssh_ports(ctx, tcp)
    notes: list[str] = []
    for st in modules:
        notes.extend(f"{st.module.name}: {n}" for n in st.notes)

    # The set: ssh first, then the modules, then extra.list (a key claimed once).
    wants: list[Want] = []
    seen: set[Key] = set()

    def want(key: Key, category: str, why: str) -> None:
        if key in seen:
            notes.append(f"{rule_text(key)} is in the set already — not added again for {category}")
            return
        seen.add(key)
        wants.append(Want(key, category, why))

    for p in ssh_ports:
        want(simple(p, "tcp"), "ssh", ssh_source)
    # Before ufw is enabled or the incoming policy changes, every port sshd really listens on
    # is opened too — SSH_PORT alone may not be where ssh is (an inactive ssh.socket, sshd
    # still on 22). Afterwards such a rule is only kept while sshd listens there.
    risky = ufw.present and not ufw.error and (
        ufw.active is False
        or ("incoming" in policy_want and ufw.policies.get("incoming") != policy_want["incoming"]))
    if risky:
        for p in live:
            if p not in ssh_ports:
                want(simple(p, "tcp"), "ssh", f"sshd listens on {p} ({live_why}) — opened before ufw is enabled "
                                              "or the incoming policy changes")
    for st in modules:
        if st.on:
            for key, why in st.keys():
                want(key, st.module.name, why)
    for ex in extras:
        if ex.key is not None:
            want(ex.key, "extra", f"{EXTRA_LIST}:{ex.line}: {ex.reason}")

    # The host's rules against the set.
    items: list[Item] = []
    by_key: dict[Key, Rule] = {}
    for r in ufw.rules:
        if r.key is not None and r.key not in by_key:
            by_key[r.key] = r
    for w in wants:
        have = by_key.get(w.key)
        if have is None:
            items.append(Item("add", w.category, "-", w.text, f"missing ({w.why})", w))
            continue
        need = families_of(w.key, ufw.ipv6)
        if ufw.families_known and not need <= have.families:
            missing = ",".join(sorted(need - have.families))
            items.append(Item("add", w.category, "-", w.text, f"the {missing} copy is missing ({w.why})", w, have))
        elif have.comment != w.comment:
            items.append(Item("adopt", w.category, "yes" if have.comment.startswith(COMMENT_PREFIX) else "no", w.text,
                              f"comment '{have.comment}' -> '{w.comment}' ({w.why})", w, have))
        else:
            items.append(Item("ok", w.category, "yes", w.text, w.why, w, have))
    wanted = {w.key for w in wants}
    # A module that is on but whose rules cannot all be written down here (its port or
    # the WAN interface unknown): a rule that is recognisably its own stays as it is.
    incomplete = {st.module.name: st for st in modules if st.on and st.incomplete}
    for r in ufw.rules:
        if r.key is not None and r.key in wanted:
            continue
        marked = r.comment.startswith(COMMENT_PREFIX)
        owner = r.comment[len(COMMENT_PREFIX):] if marked else ""
        why = ""
        mine = next((st for st in modules if r.key is not None and st.matches(r.key)), None)
        holder = mine if mine is not None and mine.module.name in incomplete else None
        if holder is None and marked:
            holder = incomplete.get(r.comment[len(COMMENT_PREFIX):])
        if holder is not None:
            items.append(Item("keep", holder.module.name, "yes" if marked else "no", r.text,
                              f"{holder.module.name} is on, but its rules cannot all be written down here "
                              f"({'; '.join(holder.notes)}) — left as it is", rule=r))
            continue
        if not marked and r.key is not None:
            for st in modules:
                if st.matches(r.key):
                    owner, why = st.module.name, f"a rule of {st.module.name}, which is {st.why}"
                    break
            else:
                for p in ssh_known:
                    if r.key in (simple(p, "tcp"), replace(simple(p, "tcp"), action="limit")):
                        owner, why = "ssh", f"an ssh rule of port {p}, which ssh does not listen on any more"
                        break
        elif marked:
            why = f"'{r.comment}' is not in the set"
        if not owner:
            items.append(Item("warn", "-", "no", r.text,
                              f"not ours (no '{COMMENT_PREFIX}' comment, not a rule of the module table) and not "
                              f"in {EXTRA_LIST} — left as it is" + (f"; comment '{r.comment}'" if r.comment else ""),
                              rule=r))
            continue
        held = protected(r.key, live)
        if held is not None:
            items.append(Item("keep", owner, "yes" if marked else "no", r.text,
                              f"{why}, but sshd listens on {held} ({live_why}) — never deleted", rule=r))
        elif not live:
            items.append(Item("keep", owner, "yes" if marked else "no", r.text,
                              f"{why}, but the port sshd listens on cannot be told ({live_why}) — nothing is deleted",
                              rule=r))
        else:
            items.append(Item("delete", owner, "yes" if marked else "no", r.text, why, rule=r))

    plan = Plan(ufw, modules, wants, items, policy_want, ssh_ports, ssh_source, live, live_why,
                [ex.closed for ex in extras if ex.closed is not None], notes)
    if with_listeners:
        check_listeners(plan, tcp)
    return plan


def check_listeners(plan: Plan, tcp: list[Listener] | None) -> None:
    """Every public TCP listener allowed or declared closed; UDP only on module ports."""
    allowed = [w.key for w in plan.wants] + [i.rule.key for i in plan.items
                                              if i.action == "keep" and i.rule is not None and i.rule.key is not None]
    closed = set(plan.closed)
    module_udp: dict[int, str] = {}
    for st in plan.modules:
        if st.port is not None and st.module.proto == "udp":
            module_udp.setdefault(st.port, st.module.name)
    udp = listeners("udp")
    plan.listeners_known = tcp is not None and udp is not None
    kernel = kernel_udp_ports()
    seen: set[tuple[str, int]] = set()

    def judge(proto: str, row: Listener, what: str) -> None:
        if (proto, row.port) in seen:
            return
        seen.add((proto, row.port))
        names = ",".join(sorted({n for n, _ in row.procs})) or what
        if any(opens(k, row.port, proto) for k in allowed):
            plan.listeners.append(ListenerItem("ok", proto, row.port, row.addr, f"{names}: allowed"))
        elif (row.port, proto) in closed:
            plan.listeners.append(ListenerItem("closed", proto, row.port, row.addr, f"{names}: declared closed in {EXTRA_LIST}"))
        else:
            plan.listeners.append(ListenerItem(
                "FAIL", proto, row.port, row.addr,
                f"{names} listens on {row.addr}:{row.port}/{proto}, which is neither allowed by the set nor declared "
                f"closed ('main|closed {row.port}/{proto}|<why>' in {EXTRA_LIST})"))

    for row in tcp or []:
        if is_public(row.addr):
            judge("tcp", row, "a process")
    for row in udp or []:
        if is_loopback(row.addr):
            continue
        if row.port in module_udp and is_public(row.addr):
            judge("udp", row, f"{module_udp[row.port]}'s port")
            continue
        if ("udp-info", row.port) in seen:
            continue
        seen.add(("udp-info", row.port))
        if row.port in kernel and not row.procs:
            what = f"listen-port of {kernel[row.port]} — kernel-owned, random"
        elif not is_public(row.addr):
            what = "on a private address (outgoing, e.g. through WARP)"
        else:
            what = ",".join(sorted({n for n, _ in row.procs})) or "no process (kernel-owned)"
        plan.listeners.append(ListenerItem("info", "udp", row.port, row.addr, f"{what} — not a module port, not checked"))


def plan_lines(ctx: Ctx, plan: Plan) -> list[str]:
    u = plan.ufw
    lines = [f"ufw={'present' if u.present else 'absent'}"]
    if u.error:
        lines.append(f"error={one(u.error)}")
    lines.append(f"active={'yes' if u.active else 'no' if u.active is not None else 'unknown'}")
    lines.append(f"ipv6={'yes' if u.ipv6 else 'no'}")
    for d in ("incoming", "outgoing", "routed"):
        want = plan.policy_want.get(d, "-")
        lines.append(f"policy={d}|{u.policies.get(d, '?')}|{want}")
    lines.append(f"ssh_ports={csv(plan.ssh_ports)}")
    lines.append(f"ssh_source={one(plan.ssh_source)}")
    lines.append(f"ssh_live={csv(plan.live)}")
    lines.append(f"ssh_live_why={one(plan.live_why)}")
    for st in plan.modules:
        lines.append(f"module={st.module.name}|{'on' if st.on else 'off'}|{one(st.why)}")
    lines.extend(i.kv() for i in plan.items)
    lines.extend(f"note={one(n)}" for n in plan.notes)
    lines.extend(x.kv() for x in plan.listeners)
    lines.append(f"listeners={'unknown' if not plan.listeners_known else 'fail' if plan.listener_failures else 'ok'}")
    lines.append(f"deadman={one(deadman_text(ctx))}")
    lines.append(
        "summary=" + " ".join(f"{a}={plan.count(a)}" for a in ("ok", "add", "adopt", "delete", "keep", "warn"))
        + f" policy_changes={len(plan.policy_changes)} enable={'yes' if u.active is False else 'no'}"
        + f" listener_failures={len(plan.listener_failures)}")
    return lines


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The dead-man (incoming policy / enable)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def load_deadman(ctx: Ctx) -> dict[str, Any] | None:
    try:
        text = read_text(ctx.host(DEADMAN_STATE))
    except Cannot:
        return None
    if not text:
        return None
    try:
        data = json.loads(text)
    except ValueError:
        return None
    return data if isinstance(data, dict) else None


def deadman_text(ctx: Ctx) -> str:
    st = load_deadman(ctx)
    if st is None:
        return "none"
    state = st.get("state")
    if state == "pending":
        return (f"PENDING CONFIRM (reverts at {st.get('deadline_iso', '?')} unless a new ssh connection from outside "
                f"on {csv(st.get('ssh_ports') or [])} or «Подтвердить» in the bot) — {describe(st)}")
    if state == "confirmed":
        return f"confirmed {st.get('done_iso', '?')} ({st.get('proof', '?')}) — {describe(st)}"
    if state == "reverted":
        return f"REVERTED {st.get('done_iso', '?')} (no proof) — {describe(st)}"
    return "none"


def describe(st: dict[str, Any]) -> str:
    parts: list[str] = []
    for c in st.get("changes") or []:
        if isinstance(c, dict):
            parts.append(f"{c.get('what')}: {c.get('from')} -> {c.get('to')}")
    return "; ".join(parts) or "?"


def timer_active() -> bool:
    out = out_of(["systemctl", "is-active", f"{DEADMAN_UNIT}.timer"])
    return (out or "").strip() == "active"


def stop_timer() -> None:
    run(["systemctl", "stop", f"{DEADMAN_UNIT}.timer"])


def self_path() -> str:
    if not SELFTEST and os.access(INSTALLED_PATH, os.X_OK):
        return INSTALLED_PATH
    return os.path.realpath(sys.argv[0])


def arm_timer() -> tuple[bool, str]:
    stop_timer()
    run(["systemctl", "reset-failed", f"{DEADMAN_UNIT}.timer", f"{DEADMAN_UNIT}.service"])
    rc, text = run(["systemd-run", "--quiet", "--collect", f"--unit={DEADMAN_UNIT}",
                    f"--on-active={DEADMAN_INTERVAL}", f"--on-unit-active={DEADMAN_INTERVAL}",
                    "--timer-property=AccuracySec=5s",
                    "--description=vpn-bot UFW dead-man (reverts the incoming policy unless proven)",
                    self_path(), "deadman-check"])
    return rc == 0, text.strip()


def journal_proof(ctx: Ctx, ports: Sequence[int], since: int) -> str:
    helper = ctx.ssh_helper
    if not ports or not helper or not os.path.isfile(helper):
        return ""
    argv = [sys.executable, "-I", helper, "--env", str(ctx.env_file), "--repo", str(ctx.repo), "--role", "main"]
    if ctx.root:
        argv += ["--root", ctx.root]
    rc, text = run([*argv, "proof-journal", "--ports", csv(ports), "--since", str(since)], timeout=180)
    if rc != 0:
        return ""
    kv = {ln.split("=", 1)[0]: ln.split("=", 1)[1] for ln in text.splitlines() if "=" in ln}
    return kv.get("proof_detail", "") if kv.get("proof") == "journal" else ""


def finish_deadman(ctx: Ctx, st: dict[str, Any], state: str, proof: str) -> None:
    stop_timer()
    data = dict(st)
    now = int(time.time())
    data.update({"state": state, "done_at": now, "done_iso": iso(now), "proof": proof or None})
    write_atomic(ctx, ctx.host(DEADMAN_STATE), json.dumps(data, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + "\n")


def revert(ctx: Ctx, st: dict[str, Any]) -> tuple[bool, list[str]]:
    """Put the incoming policy (and an inactive ufw) back as it was before the change.
    (all of it worked, what was done). Verified: the policy file and `ufw status`."""
    notes: list[str] = []
    ok = True
    prev_in = st.get("prev_incoming")
    if isinstance(prev_in, str) and prev_in in POLICIES:
        rc, text = run(["ufw", "default", prev_in, "incoming"])
        notes.append(f"ufw default {prev_in} incoming: rc {rc}" + (f" — {one(text.strip())}" if rc else ""))
        d = read_defaults(ctx)
        now = POLICY_OF_IPT.get(d.get("DEFAULT_INPUT_POLICY", "").upper(), "?")
        if rc != 0 or now != prev_in:
            ok = False
    if st.get("prev_active") is False:
        rc, text = run(["ufw", "disable"])
        notes.append(f"ufw disable (it was inactive before): rc {rc}" + (f" — {one(text.strip())}" if rc else ""))
        rc2, status_text = run(["ufw", "status"])
        if rc != 0 or rc2 != 0 or not re.search(r"^Status: inactive", status_text, re.M):
            ok = False
    return ok, notes


def deadman_check(ctx: Ctx) -> int:
    with lock(ctx):
        st = load_deadman(ctx)
        if st is None or st.get("state") != "pending":
            stop_timer()
            print("vpn-bot-ufw-apply: no UFW change waits for a proof")
            return 0
        armed = int(st.get("armed_at") or 0)
        deadline = int(st.get("deadline") or 0)
        proof = ""
        bc = st.get("bot_confirm")
        if isinstance(bc, dict) and int(bc.get("at") or 0) >= armed:
            proof = f"bot: superadmin {bc.get('admin_id')} pressed «Подтвердить» ({iso(int(bc.get('at') or 0))})"
        if not proof:
            ports = sorted({*(int(p) for p in st.get("ssh_ports") or []), *live_ssh_ports(ctx, listeners("tcp"))[0]})
            detail = journal_proof(ctx, ports, armed)
            if detail:
                proof = f"journal: {detail}"
        if proof:
            finish_deadman(ctx, st, "confirmed", proof)
            print(f"vpn-bot-ufw-apply: UFW change confirmed ({proof}) — {describe(st)}; dead-man stopped")
            return 0
        if time.time() < deadline:
            if not timer_active():
                ok, text = arm_timer()
                print(f"vpn-bot-ufw-apply: dead-man re-armed (it was not running — a reboot?): "
                      f"{'ok' if ok else 'FAILED ' + text}")
            print(f"vpn-bot-ufw-apply: waiting for a proof until {iso(deadline)} — {describe(st)}")
            return 0
        ok, notes = revert(ctx, st)
        if not ok:
            # Still pending, the timer still running: the next check tries again.
            data = dict(st)
            data["last_error"] = f"{iso(time.time())} revert failed: {'; '.join(notes)}"
            write_atomic(ctx, ctx.host(DEADMAN_STATE), json.dumps(data, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + "\n")
            if not timer_active():
                arm_timer()
            print(f"vpn-bot-ufw-apply: FAIL: no proof by {iso(deadline)}, and the REVERT FAILED — still pending, "
                  f"retried at the next check: {'; '.join(notes)}")
            return EXIT_CANNOT
        finish_deadman(ctx, st, "reverted", "")
        print(f"vpn-bot-ufw-apply: no proof by {iso(deadline)} — REVERTED: {describe(st)}")
        for n in notes:
            print(f"vpn-bot-ufw-apply:   {n}")
        return 0


def confirm(ctx: Ctx, since: int, admin: int) -> int:
    if admin <= 0:
        raise Refused("admin id must be a positive Telegram id")
    with lock(ctx):
        st = load_deadman(ctx)
        if st is None or st.get("state") != "pending" or int(st.get("armed_at") or 0) != since:
            raise Refused(f"no UFW change armed at {since} is waiting for a proof — the button is stale")
        now = int(time.time())
        st["bot_confirm"] = {"admin_id": admin, "at": now}
        finish_deadman(ctx, st, "confirmed", f"bot: superadmin {admin} pressed «Подтвердить» ({iso(now)})")
    print(f"confirmed: {describe(st)} (superadmin {admin}); dead-man stopped")
    return 0


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# apply
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
@contextlib.contextmanager
def lock(ctx: Ctx) -> Iterator[None]:
    path = ctx.host(LOCK_FILE)
    fence(ctx, path)
    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o600)
    try:
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        yield
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


def ufw(*args: str) -> tuple[int, str]:
    return run(["ufw", *args])


def delete_argv(text: str) -> list[str]:
    """`ufw delete <rule>`; a route rule is `ufw route delete <rule>` (ufw 0.36 refuses
    `ufw delete route ...` as invalid syntax — measured)."""
    toks = shlex.split(text)
    if toks and toks[0] == "route":
        return ["route", "delete", *toks[1:]]
    return ["delete", *toks]


def fail(failures: list[str], text: str) -> None:
    failures.append(text)
    print(f"vpn-bot-ufw-apply: FAIL: {text}", flush=True)


def say(text: str) -> None:
    print(f"vpn-bot-ufw-apply: {text}", flush=True)


def apply(ctx: Ctx, ssh_given: str | None) -> int:
    with lock(ctx):
        plan = compute(ctx, ssh_given, with_listeners=False)
        u = plan.ufw
        if not u.present:
            raise Cannot("ufw is not installed on this main server — its firewall is not managed")
        if u.error:
            raise Cannot(u.error)
        failures: list[str] = []
        done = {"add": 0, "adopt": 0, "delete": 0}
        for n in plan.notes:
            say(f"note: {n}")
        # 1. What is missing, then the relabels: a port opens before anything else moves.
        for it in plan.items:
            if it.action in ("add", "adopt") and it.want is not None:
                rc, text = ufw(*shlex.split(it.want.text), "comment", it.want.comment)
                verb = "added" if it.action == "add" else "adopted"
                if rc == 0:
                    done[it.action] += 1
                    say(f"{verb} '{it.text}' ({it.want.comment}) — {it.detail}")
                else:
                    fail(failures, f"ufw {it.text} comment '{it.want.comment}' failed (rc {rc}): {one(text.strip())}")
        # 2. Policies: outgoing as it is; incoming — and enabling — under the dead-man.
        dm = load_deadman(ctx)
        pending = dm is not None and dm.get("state") == "pending"
        changes = plan.policy_changes
        if "outgoing" in changes:
            rc, text = ufw("default", changes["outgoing"][1], "outgoing")
            if rc == 0:
                say(f"default outgoing: {changes['outgoing'][0]} -> {changes['outgoing'][1]}")
            else:
                fail(failures, f"ufw default {changes['outgoing'][1]} outgoing failed (rc {rc}): {one(text.strip())}")
        risky: list[dict[str, str]] = []
        if "incoming" in changes:
            risky.append({"what": "incoming policy", "from": changes["incoming"][0], "to": changes["incoming"][1]})
        if u.active is False:
            risky.append({"what": "ufw", "from": "inactive", "to": "active"})
        rc_deadman = 0
        if risky and pending:
            say(f"a UFW change waits for its proof already ({deadman_text(ctx)}) — the policy is left as it is")
        elif risky and not plan.live:
            fail(failures, f"the port sshd listens on cannot be told ({plan.live_why}) — "
                           f"{'; '.join(c['what'] for c in risky)} NOT changed")
        elif risky:
            rc_deadman = arm_and_change(ctx, plan, risky, failures)
        # 3. Deletions last.
        for it in plan.items:
            if it.action == "delete":
                argv = delete_argv(it.text)
                rc, text = ufw(*argv)
                if rc == 0:
                    done["delete"] += 1
                    say(f"deleted '{it.text}'" + (f" ('{it.rule.comment}')" if it.rule and it.rule.comment else "")
                        + f" — {it.detail}")
                else:
                    fail(failures, f"ufw {' '.join(argv)} failed (rc {rc}): {one(text.strip())}")
            elif it.action == "keep":
                say(f"kept '{it.text}' — {it.detail}")
            elif it.action == "warn":
                say(f"WARN: '{it.text}' — {it.detail}")
        # 4. Converged?
        after = compute(ctx, ssh_given, with_listeners=False)
        left = [i for i in after.items if i.action in ("add", "adopt", "delete")]
        for i in left:
            fail(failures, f"still to {i.action}: '{i.text}' ({i.detail})")
        if after.policy_changes.get("outgoing"):
            fail(failures, f"the outgoing policy is still {after.ufw.policies.get('outgoing')}")
        summary = (f"{after.count('ok')} rule(s) in place, {done['add']} added, {done['adopt']} adopted, "
                   f"{done['delete']} deleted, {after.count('keep')} kept (ssh), {after.count('warn')} unmanaged")
        say(summary)
        if rc_deadman:
            return rc_deadman
        return EXIT_NOT_CONVERGED if failures else 0


def arm_and_change(ctx: Ctx, plan: Plan, risky: list[dict[str, str]], failures: list[str]) -> int:
    """The incoming policy / enabling, behind a dead-man that is armed FIRST."""
    now = int(time.time())
    st: dict[str, Any] = {"version": 1, "state": "pending", "armed_at": now, "armed_iso": iso(now),
          "deadline": now + DEADMAN_SECONDS, "deadline_iso": iso(now + DEADMAN_SECONDS),
          "changes": risky, "prev_incoming": plan.ufw.policies.get("incoming"),
          "prev_active": bool(plan.ufw.active), "ssh_ports": sorted({*plan.ssh_ports, *plan.live}),
          "bot_confirm": None, "proof": None, "done_at": None, "done_iso": None}
    write_atomic(ctx, ctx.host(DEADMAN_STATE), json.dumps(st, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + "\n")
    ok, text = arm_timer()
    if not ok:
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            ctx.host(DEADMAN_STATE).unlink()
        print(f"vpn-bot-ufw-apply: FAIL: the dead-man could not be armed ({text}) — "
              f"{'; '.join(c['what'] for c in risky)} NOT changed", flush=True)
        return EXIT_DEADMAN
    say(f"dead-man armed: {describe(st)} stays only with a proof by {st['deadline_iso']} "
        f"(a new ssh connection from outside on {csv(st['ssh_ports'])}, or «Подтвердить» in the bot)")
    if "incoming" in plan.policy_changes:
        want = plan.policy_changes["incoming"][1]
        rc, text = ufw("default", want, "incoming")
        if rc != 0:
            fail(failures, f"ufw default {want} incoming failed (rc {rc}): {one(text.strip())}")
        else:
            say(f"default incoming: {plan.policy_changes['incoming'][0]} -> {want}")
    if plan.ufw.active is False:
        rc, text = ufw("--force", "enable")
        if rc != 0:
            fail(failures, f"ufw --force enable failed (rc {rc}): {one(text.strip())}")
        else:
            say("ufw enabled")
    return 0


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# save / restore (deploy.sh's rollback)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def save(ctx: Ctx, d: Path) -> int:
    d.mkdir(mode=0o700, parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    (d / "files").mkdir(mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    rc, text = ufw("status")
    active: bool | None = None
    if rc == 0:
        m = re.search(r"^Status: (active|inactive)", text, re.M)
        active = None if m is None else m.group(1) == "active"
    present: dict[str, bool] = {}
    for p in (*SAVED_FILES, DEADMAN_STATE):
        src = ctx.host(p)
        dst = d / "files" / p.strip("/").replace("/", "__")
        if src.is_file():
            shutil.copy2(src, dst)
            present[p] = True
        else:
            present[p] = False
    state = {"active": active, "present": present, "timer_active": timer_active(), "at": int(time.time())}
    (d / "state.json").write_text(json.dumps(state, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    say(f"saved the UFW state ({'active' if active else 'inactive' if active is False else 'unknown'}) in {d}")
    return 0


def restore(ctx: Ctx, d: Path) -> int:
    try:
        state = json.loads((d / "state.json").read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:
        raise Cannot(f"no saved UFW state in {d}: {exc}") from exc
    with lock(ctx):
        changed: list[str] = []
        for p, was in state.get("present", {}).items():
            host = ctx.host(p)
            saved = d / "files" / p.strip("/").replace("/", "__")
            if was:
                old = saved.read_bytes()
                if not host.is_file() or host.read_bytes() != old:
                    mode = (host.stat().st_mode & 0o777) if host.is_file() else 0o640
                    write_atomic(ctx, host, old.decode("utf-8", errors="surrogateescape"), mode)
                    changed.append(p)
            elif host.exists():
                fence(ctx, host)
                host.unlink()
                changed.append(p)
        if not state.get("timer_active") and timer_active():
            stop_timer()
            changed.append(f"{DEADMAN_UNIT}.timer stopped")
        was_active = state.get("active")
        rc, text = ufw("status")
        m = re.search(r"^Status: (active|inactive)", text, re.M) if rc == 0 else None
        now_active = None if m is None else m.group(1) == "active"
        ufw_files = [c for c in changed if c in SAVED_FILES]
        if was_active is True and now_active is False:
            rc, text = ufw("--force", "enable")
            say(f"ufw enabled again (it was active): rc {rc}" + (f" — {one(text.strip())}" if rc else ""))
        elif was_active is False and now_active is True:
            rc, text = ufw("disable")
            say(f"ufw disabled again (it was inactive): rc {rc}" + (f" — {one(text.strip())}" if rc else ""))
        elif ufw_files and now_active:
            rc, text = ufw("reload")
            say(f"ufw reload: rc {rc}" + (f" — {one(text.strip())}" if rc else ""))
        say("restored: " + (", ".join(changed) if changed else "nothing had changed"))
        return 0 if rc == 0 else EXIT_CANNOT


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# status
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def status(ctx: Ctx) -> str:
    try:
        plan = compute(ctx, None, with_listeners=False)
    except (Refused, Cannot) as exc:
        return f"ufw: not judged ({exc})"
    u = plan.ufw
    if not u.present or u.error:
        return f"ufw: {u.error or 'not installed'}"
    todo = plan.count("add") + plan.count("adopt") + plan.count("delete")
    text = (f"ufw: {'active' if u.active else 'INACTIVE'}; incoming {u.policies.get('incoming')}, outgoing "
            f"{u.policies.get('outgoing')}, routed {u.policies.get('routed')} (not managed); "
            f"{plan.count('ok')} rule(s) as the repo says")
    if todo:
        text += f", {todo} to change"
    if plan.count("keep"):
        text += f", {plan.count('keep')} kept for ssh"
    if plan.count("warn"):
        text += f", {plan.count('warn')} unmanaged (WARN)"
    dm = deadman_text(ctx)
    if dm != "none":
        text += f"; dead-man: {dm}"
    return text


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Commands
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
WRITING_COMMANDS = frozenset({"apply", "save", "restore", "deadman-check", "confirm"})
GLOBAL_OPTIONS_WITH_VALUE = frozenset({"--env", "--repo", "--root", "--ssh-port-helper"})


def subcommand(argv: Sequence[str]) -> str:
    skip = False
    for tok in argv:
        if skip:
            skip = False
        elif tok in GLOBAL_OPTIONS_WITH_VALUE:
            skip = True
        elif not tok.startswith("-"):
            return tok
    return ""


def host_mount_namespace_argv(argv: Sequence[str]) -> list[str] | None:
    """The argv to re-run this helper in PID 1's mount namespace, or None when it already
    runs there (the same escape as scripts/vpn-bot-ssh-port)."""
    if SELFTEST or os.geteuid() != 0 or os.environ.get("VPN_BOT_UFW_HOSTNS") == "1":
        return None
    if subcommand(argv) not in WRITING_COMMANDS:
        return None
    try:
        if os.readlink("/proc/self/ns/mnt") == os.readlink("/proc/1/ns/mnt"):
            return None
    except OSError:
        return None
    return ["nsenter", "--mount=/proc/1/ns/mnt", "--", sys.executable, "-I", os.path.realpath(sys.argv[0]), *argv]


def make_ctx(args: argparse.Namespace) -> Ctx:
    root = (args.root or "").rstrip("/")
    if SELFTEST and not root:
        raise Cannot("VPN_BOT_UFW_SELFTEST=1 needs --root")
    env_file = Path(args.env or APP_DIR + "/.env")
    # Under the test seam only an explicitly named SSH port helper runs: the installed one
    # may exist on the production host the suite runs on.
    default_helper = "" if SELFTEST else SSH_PORT_HELPER
    ctx = Ctx(env_file=env_file, repo=Path(args.repo or APP_DIR), root=root,
              ssh_helper=args.ssh_port_helper if args.ssh_port_helper is not None else default_helper)
    ctx.env_text = read_text(env_file) or ""
    role = ctx.env("NODE_ROLE")
    if role not in ("", "main"):
        raise Refused(f"NODE_ROLE={role!r}: UFW is the main server's firewall (a relay has vpnrelay_input)")
    return ctx


def require_root(cmd: str) -> None:
    if not SELFTEST and os.geteuid() != 0:
        raise Cannot(f"{cmd} must run as root (sudo -n {INSTALLED_PATH} {cmd} ...)")


def main(argv: Sequence[str]) -> int:
    reexec = host_mount_namespace_argv(argv)
    if reexec is not None:
        os.environ["VPN_BOT_UFW_HOSTNS"] = "1"
        try:
            os.execvpe(reexec[0], reexec, os.environ)  # noqa: S606 — fixed argv: nsenter, this interpreter, this script
        except OSError as exc:
            print(f"vpn-bot-ufw-apply: cannot enter the host mount namespace ({exc}) — going on in this one",
                  file=sys.stderr)
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="vpn-bot-ufw-apply", description="UFW of the main server (docs/host-state.md)")
    ap.add_argument("--env")
    ap.add_argument("--repo")
    ap.add_argument("--root")
    ap.add_argument("--ssh-port-helper")
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)
    for name in ("plan", "apply", "listeners"):
        p = sub.add_parser(name)
        p.add_argument("--ssh-ports", default=None)
    sub.add_parser("status")
    sub.add_parser("deadman-check")
    for name in ("save", "restore"):
        p = sub.add_parser(name)
        p.add_argument("--dir", required=True)
    p = sub.add_parser("confirm")
    p.add_argument("--since", required=True, type=int)
    p.add_argument("--admin", required=True, type=int)
    args = ap.parse_args(argv)
    try:
        ctx = make_ctx(args)
        if args.cmd == "plan":
            try:
                plan = compute(ctx, args.ssh_ports)
            except Refused as exc:
                print("result=refused")
                print("error=" + str(exc).replace("\n", " ").replace("\r", " "))   # not split on '|'
                return EXIT_REFUSED
            print("\n".join(plan_lines(ctx, plan)))
            print("result=ok")
            return 0
        if args.cmd == "listeners":
            plan = compute(ctx, args.ssh_ports)
            for x in plan.listeners:
                print(x.kv())
            bad = plan.listener_failures
            print(f"listeners={'unknown' if not plan.listeners_known else 'fail' if bad else 'ok'}")
            if not plan.listeners_known:
                print("vpn-bot-ufw-apply: `ss` failed — the listeners are not checked", file=sys.stderr)
                return EXIT_CANNOT
            return EXIT_NOT_CONVERGED if bad else 0
        if args.cmd == "status":
            print(status(ctx))
            return 0
        require_root(args.cmd)
        if args.cmd == "apply":
            return apply(ctx, args.ssh_ports)
        if args.cmd == "save":
            return save(ctx, Path(args.dir))
        if args.cmd == "restore":
            return restore(ctx, Path(args.dir))
        if args.cmd == "deadman-check":
            return deadman_check(ctx)
        if args.cmd == "confirm":
            return confirm(ctx, args.since, args.admin)
    except Refused as exc:
        print(f"vpn-bot-ufw-apply: {exc}", file=sys.stderr)
        return EXIT_REFUSED
    except (Cannot, OSError) as exc:
        print(f"vpn-bot-ufw-apply: {exc}", file=sys.stderr)
        return EXIT_CANNOT
    return 2


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
